// The CLI-owned CENSUS, ruled BY NAME (adversarial round 8).
//
// Maintainer-owned, checked in, consumed only by
// scripts/claude-authority-classification.mjs, which composes each row into an
// exact ruling. Nothing in src/ imports this file.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
// -------------------
// The exact-ruling rule says a name in one of the CLI's own namespaces is
// never settled by a pattern: each gets an individual ruling and an individual
// reason, and a new one is a hard failure until someone writes it. Until round
// 8 the generator asked that question only of names that were also
// AUTHORITY-SHAPED, so 611 names in those namespaces were counted, digested
// and never ruled -- and one of them, CLAUDE_BRIDGE_REATTACH_OWNER_ACCT, is the
// account half of an identity pair whose organization half the manifest
// already stripped. A shape pattern is a denylist of shapes, and four rounds
// each found a shape it lacked (RATE_LIMIT, ENV_SCRUB, _OVERRIDES, ACCT). The
// gate now asks about EVERY CLI-owned census name, and this file answers.
//
// HOW EACH ROW WAS DECIDED
// ------------------------
// Pinned: Claude Code 2.1.278, win32-x64, sha256 006ea5c8...cced8. Every name
// was ruled against that binary by an independent reviewer who read each
// occurrence (up to six, with 240 bytes of context either side) and, where
// that was not enough, the surrounding code -- then re-checked by the
// adversarial pass. The excerpts are NOT committed: the binary is proprietary
// and is never vendored, excerpted or quoted here. What is committed is the
// reviewer's finding -- the second element of each row -- which is the reason
// the manifest carries. The test is D3: does an inherited value select or
// override the account, the credential source, the provider, the provider
// endpoint, or the realm root? Only one did.
//
// A row is [kind, what]. `kind` is one of the classification module's kinds;
// `what` says what the CLI does with an inherited value, specifically enough
// that the ruling can be re-argued from the row rather than re-derived from
// the binary. "NOT read as a variable:" marks a name that occurs only as a
// key in the CLI's typed env-schema map, a label, or a constant in this build;
// it is ruled anyway, because a later build may add the read.
//
// A new CLI version that adds a CLAUDE_/ANTHROPIC_/ANT_/CCR_/... name fails the
// generator until a row is added HERE (or an exact ruling in the classification
// module, which wins on collision -- see the assertion there).

/** Names that end in `_` are PREFIX FRAGMENTS of names the CLI assembles at
 *  run time (a `startsWith` sweep, a scrub list). They are not variables and
 *  are not ruled; the generator records them in `provenance.census.fragments`
 *  so the residual "a name assembled at run time is invisible to a literal
 *  scan" is stated with the prefixes it is known to hide behind. */
export const CLI_OWNED_CENSUS_FRAGMENTS = Object.freeze([
  "ANTHROPIC_",
  "CLAUDE_",
  "CLAUDE_BG_",
  "CLAUDE_CODE_",
  "CLAUDE_CODE_HOST_",
  "CLAUDE_CODE_RELAUNCH_",
  "CLAUDE_CODE_SDK_",
  "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_",
])

